depgraph: replay _iter_similar_available lazily inside the probe loop

Sub-series: A (probe, match and config memos) - patch 4 of 10; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Of these it needs 0001 only.
Ported to upstream 73646c35d: adapted: _iter_similar_available() has a new parameter selectable_built there; it is passed on to _iter_similar_available_imp(), and a call with selectable_built is neither answered from the probe memo nor recorded in it (its only caller, _slot_confict_backtrack, runs outside the probe loop)

Over 0004 (three states): start 103.7 -> 98.6, masks 67.9 -> 62.6,
base 23.6 -> 22.5; under 1.5 s per state once patch 0002 is applied.
Does NOT apply to upstream head: the function gained a parameter there.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20. Not a human-written
change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on six states of
one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the same merge list
in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts and the same
package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
